course: dictionary
lesson: 2827
title: Divide: share, split and separate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Divide means to split a number or amount into equal parts or groups. The sign for dividing is ÷, so «divide 12 by 3» means share 12 into 3 equal groups, which gives 4 in each group.
explain: Divide can also mean to split things into parts, as in «divide the class into teams», or to keep two places apart, as in «a river divides the town». Read the words around divide to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Dividing is the opposite of multiplying, so it can undo a step. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: if sharing or splitting makes sense there, you have the right meaning.
fact: Divide means to split a number or amount into equal parts or groups.
fact: The sign for dividing is ÷, and «divide A by B» means A ÷ B.
fact: Dividing is the opposite of multiplying, so it can undo a multiplication.
fact: Divide can mean to split things into parts, as in «divide the class into teams».
fact: Divide can also mean to keep two places apart, as in «a river divides the town».
exercise: «To find a fraction of a quantity, first find one equal part: divide by the number below the line.» What does divide mean here? | Add the numbers together | Take a photo of the number | Make the number bigger | *Split into equal parts
exercise: «A river divides the town in two.» What does divides mean? | Makes the town smaller | Washes the town away | Joins the two parts into one | *Keeps the two parts apart
exercise: Which operation undoes multiplying? | *Dividing | Rounding | Making it bigger | Adding
test: «Undo the steps from the end: take away the 5 to get 21, then divide by 3 to get 7.» Jamal has 7 and must undo dividing by 3. What should he do to 7? | Subtract 3 | Divide by 3 again | Add 5 | *Multiply by 3
test: «Divide the class into teams.» What does divide mean here? | Lose the way | *Split into groups | Join together | Sing a song
exam: «x % 2 is the remainder after dividing by 2, and // divides and drops the remainder.» What does // do to a number? | Makes it equal to zero | Keeps the remainder and adds it on | *Divides it and drops the remainder | Multiplies it by two
